It gives you magic resistance.  Magic resistance is a binary toggle.
You either have it or you don't.  If you have it, you are safe from
teleport, level teleport and polymorph traps, wands of magic missle,
striking and death and from finger of death.  And maybe a thing or
two more.  MR is provided by cloaks of magic resistance, grey dragon
scale mail and a by a handful of artifacts such as the PYEC.

It does not provide magic cancellation.  Magic cancellation comes
in a range of values from 0 to 3 and is generally conferred by body
armor and cloaks.  Magic cancellation protects against level
draining attacks with a percentage chance to avoid the level
drain.  At level 3, its something like 99% defense.  I'm not sure what
other special attacks are foiled with magic cancellation.  I had
thought that cockatrice stoning was affected, but that appears
to have been an unfounded rumor.

The PYEC is referred to as "unreliable" because certain monsters, most
notably the Wizard, can steal the PYEC. If it is serving as
your only source of magic resistance, a follow-up finger of death
is likely to be inconvenient.

